  "term": "brainstem auditory evoked response",
  "definition": "Brainstem auditory evoked response is an objective neurological test that measures how the auditory pathways in the brainstem respond to sound. It is used to assess hearing pathway function from the auditory nerve to the midbrain and to help identify suspected abnormalities involving the eighth cranial nerve or related pathways.",
